Hi,
> Stefan,
> Bruno is correct, the PCI config space should be saved and restored by
> the driver's suspend and resume routines.  suspend/resume routines
> typically do other hardware dependent stuff, but your debugging suggests
> that at least for some of these devices, simply saving and restoring pci
> config space (pci_save_state()/pci_restore_state()) may be sufficient.

I had a look at the drivers and most of them don't have 
pci_save_state()/pci_restore_state() calls.
The sound driver calls pci_save_state()/pci_restore_state(), but this calls 
cause a lockup. I commented out some code and  found out that any call to 
pci_enable_device(), pci_restore_state() and pci_write_config_XXXX() causes a 
lockup.
Why doesn't setpci crash?

I fear I have to add the calls manually in every driver.

/Stefan


